WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.418
His rookie year I knew
he was a baller

00:00:01.418 --> 00:00:03.086
because he was lettin'
our sideline know

00:00:03.086 --> 00:00:05.338
how much money he
had in the bank already.

00:00:05.338 --> 00:00:07.090
He was lettin' us know
he was the man

00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:09.175
cuz he's a top-10 pick,
right?

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:09.342
cuz he's a top-10 pick,
right?

00:00:09.342 --> 00:00:10.677
- What'd you go? 8?

00:00:10.677 --> 00:00:12.262
- Yeah, I went 8.
- How was draft for you?

00:00:12.262 --> 00:00:13.888
- Yeah, that's what
I wanna hear, the draft.

00:00:13.888 --> 00:00:16.266
The lead-up to that.
- Draft was amazing, man.

00:00:16.266 --> 00:00:17.809
- Yeah, 2004, the draft.

00:00:17.809 --> 00:00:19.728
- Yeah, 2004,
and that was back when

00:00:19.728 --> 00:00:22.564
you know, they only took
about the top five guys.

00:00:22.564 --> 00:00:25.734
You know, I'm in the room
with guys like Eli Manning

00:00:25.734 --> 00:00:28.194
who's supposed
to be No. 1 overall

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:30.739
and Big Ben and Robert Gallery.

00:00:30.739 --> 00:00:33.616
And I'm like, "Dude, I don't
care if I sit in that green room

00:00:33.616 --> 00:00:35.326
and I am the last one.

00:00:35.326 --> 00:00:37.954
I want to share
in this experience."

00:00:37.954 --> 00:00:39.914
And, you know,
we had a running joke, like

00:00:39.914 --> 00:00:42.000
"Who's gonna be
the last guy drafted?"

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:43.126
And, you know, I wasn't upset.

00:00:43.126 --> 00:00:43.543
And, you know, I wasn't upset.

00:00:43.543 --> 00:00:45.587
I said, "I'm gonna be
the last one.

00:00:45.587 --> 00:00:47.213
I know I'm goin' 10 to Houston."

00:00:47.213 --> 00:00:49.549
So everyone kinda
has their own table.

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:50.967
When you haven't been drafted

00:00:50.967 --> 00:00:52.969
you're sitting back
watching this unfold.

00:00:52.969 --> 00:00:54.012
- Right.
- And so, yeah

00:00:54.012 --> 00:00:55.930
with Eli, San Diego drafts him—

00:00:55.930 --> 00:00:57.432
- Yes, they did.
- Before they actually

00:00:57.432 --> 00:00:58.808
figure out the trade.

00:00:58.808 --> 00:01:01.352
We literally sat back
and watched him

00:01:01.352 --> 00:01:04.647
not wanna hold the jersey,
not wanna put the hat on.

00:01:04.647 --> 00:01:06.524
He's just in there, pissed.

00:01:06.524 --> 00:01:09.444
And so as the draft's
kinda goin' on

00:01:09.444 --> 00:01:11.529
guys are gettin' called,
guys are gettin' called.

00:01:11.529 --> 00:01:14.491
Me and Ben are last,
and I'm just thinkin', you know

00:01:14.491 --> 00:01:15.867
"All right, Ben's gonna go"

00:01:15.867 --> 00:01:17.994
and I had actually went
to the bathroom

00:01:17.994 --> 00:01:19.704
and then I hear my name, "8."

00:01:19.704 --> 00:01:22.749
And, you know, as I'm hugging
my mom and kissing her

00:01:22.749 --> 00:01:24.709
and dappin' up my brothers
and stuff

00:01:24.709 --> 00:01:27.712
I just kind of look over at Ben
and, like, "I guess you last."

00:01:27.712 --> 00:01:30.048
You know, just kinda,
kind of a running joke

00:01:30.048 --> 00:01:31.674
to this day, but—
- Ah, that's awesome.

00:01:31.674 --> 00:01:33.885
- Heck, he probably went
in the best spot

00:01:33.885 --> 00:01:37.138
because he has two rings,
he went to a great defense

00:01:37.138 --> 00:01:39.057
great organization and so—

00:01:39.057 --> 00:01:42.352
Everything happens for a reason,
but I was not the last one

00:01:42.352 --> 00:01:46.231
even though all week long
that's all we joked about.

